:Class Message
⍝ Composes the text of an email from an instance of `ConnectionParameters` and an instance of `MailParameters`.
⍝ Instances are created by `Connection.Send`; there is usually no need to create one yourself.
    :Field public From←''
    :Field public Subject←''
    :Field public ReplyTo←''
    :Field public Org←''
    :Field public To←''           ⍝ vector of email addresses
    :Field public CC←''           ⍝ vector of email addresses
    :Field public BCC←''          ⍝ vector of email addresses
    :Field public Headers←''      ⍝ vector of ('name' 'value')
    :Field public XMailer←''
    :Field public Body←''         ⍝ character vector 'content' or vector of ('MIMEType' 'content')
    :Field public Attachments←''  ⍝ vector of instances of the `Attachment` class.
    :Field public Client          ⍝ reference to SMTP client that created this

    :Field _text←''
    :Field _recipients←''

    :Property Text
    :Access public
        ∇ r←Get
          r←_text
        ∇
    :EndProperty

    :Property Recipients
    :Access public
        ∇ r←Get
          r←_recipients
        ∇
    :EndProperty

    ∇ make1(_Client connectionParams mailParams)
      :Access public
      :Implements constructor
      Client←_Client
      XMailer←connectionParams.XMailer
      ReplyTo←connectionParams.ReplyTo
      Org←connectionParams.Org
      From←mailParams.From
      Subject←mailParams.Subject
      Body←mailParams.Body
      CC←mailParams.CC
      BCC←mailParams.BCC
      Attachments←mailParams.Attachments
    ∇

    ∇ (rc msg text)←Compose mailParams;haveAtts;boundary;mime;i;att;invalid;nonASCII
    ⍝ Composes the email: headers, body and attachments.
    ⍝ Returns `rc` (0 for success, ¯1 otherwise), an error message (empty for success) and the composed text.
    ⍝ The text consists of characters in the range 0-255 (UTF-8 bytes) with CRLF line ends.
    ⍝ It is not dot-stuffed yet; `Connection.Send` does that with `DotStuff` right before sending it.
      :Access public
      (rc msg text)←¯1 '' ''
      _recipients←CompileAllRecipients mailParams
      :If 0<≢invalid←InvalidAddresses mailParams
          msg←'Invalid email address: ',⊃{⍺,', ',⍵}/invalid
          →Exit
      :EndIf
      :If 0<≢nonASCII←NonASCIIAddresses mailParams
          msg←'Email address with characters other than ASCII (not supported): ',⊃{⍺,', ',⍵}/nonASCII
          →Exit
      :EndIf
      text←'Date: ',now,CRLF
      text,←'From'AddressHeader From
      text,←'Reply-To'AddressHeader ReplyTo
      text,←'Organization'TextHeader Org
      text,←'X-Mailer'TextHeader XMailer
      text,←'MIME-Version: 1.0',CRLF
      text,←'To:'CompileRecipients Recipients
      text,←'CC:'CompileRecipients Recipients
      text,←'Subject'TextHeader Subject

      :If haveAtts←0≠≢Attachments
          boundary←'000',((⍕⎕TS)~' '),'APLTeamSMTP'
          text,←'Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="',boundary,'"',CRLF
          text,←CRLF
          text,←'This is a multi-part message in MIME format.',CRLF
          text,←'--',boundary,CRLF
      :EndIf

      :If 0≠≢Body
          mime←(1+∨/'<html'⍷⎕C⊃Body)⊃'plain' 'html'
          text,←'Content-Type: text/',mime,'; charset="UTF-8"',CRLF
          text,←CRLF
          text,←EncodeBody Body
          text,←CRLF
      :EndIf

      :If haveAtts
          :For i :In ⍳≢Attachments
              (msg att)←ProcessAttachment i⊃Attachments
              :If 0<≢msg
                  msg←'Error processing attachment ',(⍕i),': ',msg
                  →Exit
              :EndIf
              text,←'--',boundary,CRLF
              text,←att
          :EndFor
          text,←'--',boundary,'--',CRLF
      :EndIf
      (rc msg)←0 ''
      _text←text
     Exit:
    ∇

    ∇ (msg r)←ProcessAttachment attachment;mimeType;content;filename;path;qdmx
    ⍝ Returns the MIME part for `attachment`, an instance of the `Attachment` class.
    ⍝ `msg` is empty for success; otherwise it says why the file could not be read, and `r` is empty.
      (msg r)←'' ''
      (path mimeType)←attachment.(filename mimeType)
      filename←⎕UCS'UTF-8'⎕UCS(∊¯2↑⎕NPARTS path)~⎕UCS 10 13 34   ⍝ No line breaks and no double quotes in a header
      :Trap 19 22
          content←ReadFile path
      :Else
          qdmx←⎕DMX
          msg←'cannot read file "',path,'": ',qdmx.EM,{0=≢⍵:'' ⋄ ' (',⍵,')'}3⊃qdmx.OSError
          :Return
      :EndTrap
      r,←'Content-Type: ',mimeType,'; charset="US-ASCII"; name="',filename,'"',CRLF
      r,←'Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="',filename,'"',CRLF
      r,←'Content-Transfer-Encoding: base64',CRLF,CRLF
      r,←chunk Base64Encoding content
    ∇

    ∇ r←ReadFile file;tno
     ⍝ We don't trap errors here because we don't want to pretend sending emails with attachments when we don't
      tno←file ⎕NTIE 0
      r←⎕NREAD tno,(⎕DR' '),¯1 0
      ⎕NUNTIE tno
    ∇

    ∇ r←CompileAllRecipients mailParams;addrs
      r←''
      r,←⊂'To: ',normalizeAddr mailParams.To
      r,←{0=≢⍵:⍵ ⋄ 'CC: '∘,¨normalizeAddr¨⍵}mailParams.CC
      r,←{0=≢⍵:⍵ ⋄ 'BCC: '∘,¨normalizeAddr¨⍵}mailParams.BCC
    ∇

    ∇ r←InvalidAddresses mailParams
    ⍝ Returns those of From, Reply-To, To, CC and BCC that `extractAddr` cannot find an email address in.
      r←(From ReplyTo),(⊂mailParams.To),mailParams.CC,mailParams.BCC
      r←r/⍨0<≢¨r~¨' '
      r←r/⍨0=≢¨extractAddr¨r
    ∇

    ∇ r←NonASCIIAddresses mailParams
    ⍝ Returns those of From, Reply-To, To, CC and BCC whose email address (not the display name) has
    ⍝ characters above ⎕UCS 127. Such an address would need the SMTPUTF8 extension, which is not supported.
      r←(From ReplyTo),(⊂mailParams.To),mailParams.CC,mailParams.BCC
      r←r/⍨0<≢¨r~¨' '
      r←r/⍨{∨/127<⎕UCS extractAddr ⍵}¨r
    ∇

    ∇ r←CRLF
      r←⎕UCS 13 10
    ∇

    ∇ r←EncodeBody body;lines
    ⍝ `body` is a vector of character vectors, each of which may contain line breaks itself.
    ⍝ Returns the body as UTF-8 bytes (as characters), every line ending with CRLF.
    ⍝ A lone CR or a lone LF is turned into CRLF as well: SMTP knows no other line end, and some servers
    ⍝ treat a lone LF as one, which would make dot-stuffing incomplete.
      lines←⊃,/SplitLines¨body
      r←⎕UCS'UTF-8'⎕UCS∊lines,¨⊂CRLF
    ∇

    ∇ r←SplitLines text;cr;lf
      :Access Public Shared
    ⍝ Splits the character vector `text` at CRLF, at a lone CR and at a lone LF.
    ⍝ Empty lines are kept, so 'a',CRLF,CRLF,'b' results in 'a' '' 'b'.
      cr←⎕UCS 13
      lf←⎕UCS 10
      text←(~(cr=text)∧1↓(lf=text),0)/text   ⍝ CRLF → LF
      ((cr=text)/text)←lf                     ⍝ Lone CR → LF
      r←1↓¨(lf=lf,text)⊂lf,text
    ∇

    ∇ r←DotStuff text;mask
      :Access Public Shared
    ⍝ `text` is the composed message: lines separated by CRLF.
    ⍝ Doubles the dot at the start of every line that starts with a dot (RFC 5321, section 4.5.2).
    ⍝ Without this, a line consisting of a single dot would end the message early, and the server would
    ⍝ take whatever follows for SMTP commands. The receiving server removes the extra dots again.
      mask←('.'=text)∧¯1↓1,(⎕UCS 10)=text
      r←(1+mask)/text
    ∇

    ∇ r←chunk base64
    ⍝ Returns the base64-encoded text `base64` as lines of at most 72 characters, each one ending with CRLF.
    ⍝ RFC 2045 allows up to 76 characters. base64 has no dots, so no line needs dot-stuffing.
      r←CRLF
      :If 0<≢base64
          r←∊(base64⊂⍨(≢base64)⍴72↑1),¨⊂CRLF
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←extractAddr addr;quotes;ind;del
      :Access Public Shared
        ⍝ extract the mail address from a string
        ⍝ perform very cursory validation on the address
        ⍝ addr - the string to be validated (can be in form "Fred Bloggs" fred@bloggs.com)
        ⍝ r    - the email address or empty if not valid
        ⍝ The domain part does not need a dot, so an internal address like `kai@localhost` is accepted.
      r←''
      quotes←(⊢∨≠\)'"'=addr ⍝ mask out quoted material e.g. "fred@work" fred@bloggs.com
      ind←⊃⍸quotes<addr='@'
      :If ind≠0
          del←0,(1+≢addr),⍨⍸quotes<' '=addr ⍝ break on space
          r←addr{⍵[1]↓(¯1+⍵[2])↑⍺}del[0 1+del⍸ind]
          r←⊃('^<?[^<>@\s]+@[^<>@\s.][^<>@\s]*>?$'⎕S'%')r
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ addr←normalizeAddr addr;a
      :Access Public Shared
    ⍝ Returns `addr` with the email address in angle brackets: 'Fred fred@b.com' becomes 'Fred <fred@b.com>'.
    ⍝ An `addr` that `extractAddr` finds no email address in is returned unchanged.
      :If 0<≢addr~' '  ⍝ MB: avoid issues when addr is a 0/ManyAddrs
      :AndIf 0<≢a←extractAddr addr
          :If '<>'≢(⊣/,⊢/)a
              addr←(addr/⍨~∨\⌽<\⌽a⍷addr),'<',a,'>'
          :EndIf
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←Base64Encoding txt;⎕IO;A;ed
      :Access Public Shared
        ⍝ ⍵ byte string: 256∧.>⎕ucs ⍵
        ⍝ ← longer (4:3) string in A-Z,a-z,0-9,+/= only
        ⍝ Text that may contain characters above ⎕UCS 127 must be converted to UTF-8 first.
      ⎕IO←0
      A←'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/'
      ed←{⊃⍵{⍺{2⊥⍉((⌈(⍴⍵)÷⍺),⍺){⍺⍴(×/⍺)↑⍵}⍵},⍉(⍵⍴2)⊤⍺⍺}/⍺}
      r←{⍵,'='⍴⍨4|-⍴⍵}(⊂6 8 ed ⎕UCS txt)⌷A
    ∇

    ∇ r←EncodedWords text;word;c
      :Access Public Shared
    ⍝ Returns `text` as a vector of RFC 2047 encoded words (UTF-8, base64).
    ⍝ Each word holds at most 39 bytes of UTF-8, so it is at most 64 characters long and fits on a header
    ⍝ line together with the header name. Characters are never split across two words.
      r←''
      word←''
      :For c :In text
          :If 39<≢'UTF-8'⎕UCS word,c
              r,←⊂word
              word←''
          :EndIf
          word,←c
      :EndFor
      r,←⊂word
      r←{'=?utf-8?B?',(Base64Encoding ⎕UCS'UTF-8'⎕UCS ⍵),'?='}¨r
    ∇

    ∇ r←name TextHeader value
      :Access Public Shared
    ⍝ Returns a header line for an unstructured header like "Subject", ending with CRLF, or '' when `value` is empty.
    ⍝ A value with characters above ⎕UCS 127 is sent as RFC 2047 encoded words, one per line.
    ⍝ An ASCII value that would make the line longer than 78 characters is folded at blanks (RFC 5322, section 2.2.3).
      r←''
      :If 0<≢value~' '
          :If ∨/127<⎕UCS value
              r←name,': ',⊃{⍺,CRLF,' ',⍵}/EncodedWords value
          :Else
              r←name,': ',value
              :If 78<≢r
              :AndIf ' '∊value
                  r←name FoldAtBlanks value
              :EndIf
          :EndIf
          r,←CRLF
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←name FoldAtBlanks value;line;w
    ⍝ Returns "name: value" with CRLF inserted in front of blanks so that no line exceeds 78 characters,
    ⍝ unless a single word is longer than that. Consecutive blanks are reduced to one.
      r←''
      line←name,':'
      :For w :In ' '(≠⊆⊢)value
          :If 78<(≢line)+1+≢w
          :AndIf ' '∊line                             ⍝ At least one word on this line already
              r,←line,CRLF
              line←''
          :EndIf
          line,←' ',w
      :EndFor
      r,←line
    ∇

    ∇ r←EncodeAddress addr;ind;name;a
      :Access Public Shared
    ⍝ `addr` is an address as returned by `normalizeAddr`, for example 'Kai Jäger <kai@aplteam.com>'.
    ⍝ A display name with characters above ⎕UCS 127 is sent as RFC 2047 encoded words.
    ⍝ The address itself is never encoded that way: mail servers would not recognise it anymore.
      ind←1+(≢addr)-(⌽addr)⍳'<'
      :If ind>≢addr                                 ⍝ No angle brackets: a bare address
          r←⎕UCS'UTF-8'⎕UCS addr
      :Else
          name←{(+/∧\' '=⍵)↓⍵}{(-+/∧\' '=⌽⍵)↓⍵}(ind-1)↑addr
          a←⎕UCS'UTF-8'⎕UCS(ind-1)↓addr
          :If ∨/127<⎕UCS name
              name←{'""'≡(⊣/,⊢/)⍵:¯1↓1↓⍵ ⋄ ⍵}name
              name←⊃{⍺,CRLF,' ',⍵}/EncodedWords name
          :EndIf
          r←name,((0<≢name)/' '),a
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←name AddressHeader addr
    ⍝ Returns a header line for a header like "From" that carries a single address, or '' when `addr` is empty.
      r←''
      :If 0<≢addr~' '
          r←name,': ',(EncodeAddress normalizeAddr addr),CRLF
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←now
    ⍝ Returns the current local time as an RFC 5322 date, for example "Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:46:52 +0100".
    ⍝ The offset from UTC is rounded to full minutes, so zones like India (+0530) come out right.
      r←FormatDate ⎕TS(⌊0.5+1440×(1 ⎕DT'J')-1 ⎕DT'Z')
    ∇

    ∇ r←FormatDate(ts offset);two
      :Access Public Shared
    ⍝ `ts` is a timestamp in `⎕TS` format (at least 6 items), `offset` the number of minutes east of UTC.
    ⍝ Returns an RFC 5322 date, for example "Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:46:52 +0100".
      two←{¯2↑'0',⍕⍵}
      r←(1+7|⊃1 ⎕DT⊂3↑ts)⊃'Sun' 'Mon' 'Tue' 'Wed' 'Thu' 'Fri' 'Sat'
      r,←', ',(⍕ts[3]),' ',(ts[2]⊃'Jan' 'Feb' 'Mar' 'Apr' 'May' 'Jun' 'Jul' 'Aug' 'Sep' 'Oct' 'Nov' 'Dec')
      r,←' ',(⍕ts[1]),' ',(two ts[4]),':',(two ts[5]),':',(two ts[6])
      r,←' ',('+-'[1+offset<0]),(two⌊(|offset)÷60),two 60||offset
    ∇

    ∇ r←Config
        ⍝ returns current message configuration
      :Access public
      r←↑{⍵(⍎⍵)}¨⎕THIS⍎'⎕NL ¯2.2 ¯2.3'
    ∇

    ∇ r←type CompileRecipients recipients;addrs;len;i;a
    ⍝ Returns the header line for `type` ("To:" or "CC:"), ending with CRLF, or '' when there is no such recipient.
    ⍝ `recipients` is what `CompileAllRecipients` returns, for example:
    ⍝ 'CC:'CompileRecipients 'To: <kai@aplteam.com>' 'CC: <info@tatin.dev>' 'CC: <john-doe@myserver.com>'
    ⍝ ←→ 'CC: <info@tatin.dev>, <john-doe@myserver.com>',CRLF
    ⍝ A line that would get longer than 78 characters is folded after a comma (RFC 5322, section 2.2.3).
      'Left argument is invalid: must be either "To:" or "CC:"'⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨~(⊂type)∊'To:' 'CC:'
      addrs←recipients/⍨(⊂type)≡¨(≢type)↑¨recipients
      addrs←{⍵↓⍨⍵⍳' '}¨addrs
      addrs←addrs/⍨0<≢¨addrs~¨' '
      r←''
      :If 0<≢addrs
          addrs←EncodeAddress¨addrs
          r←type
          len←≢r
          :For i :In ⍳≢addrs
              a←(i⊃addrs),(i<≢addrs)/','
              :If (1<i)∧78<len+1+≢a
                  r,←CRLF
                  len←0
              :EndIf
              r,←' ',a
              len+←1+≢a
          :EndFor
          r,←CRLF
      :EndIf
    ∇

:EndClass
